Third-party resources referenced by the framework
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No third-party dataset is bundled with this release. The resources below are
read by the construction chain at run time, from their own distribution
points, under their own terms. Each entry states the version the manuscript
names, the access route, and the licence the distributor publishes. Where the
licence is not stated by the distributor, that is recorded as "not stated".

HGNC (HUGO Gene Nomenclature Committee)
  Version     : 2021 release, as cited in the manuscript
  Access      : https://www.genenames.org
  Licence     : CC0 1.0 Universal for the gene nomenclature records; the
                HGNC symbol list is redistributed under the same terms.
  Used for    : gene and protein-coding-locus identity.

DrugBank
  Version     : DrugBank 5.0, as cited in the manuscript
  Access      : https://go.drugbank.com
  Licence     : Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 for the open
                release; the full release requires a licence and is not
                redistributed here.
  Used for    : compound identity, mechanism and drug-target relations.

KEGG
  Version     : KEGG pathway release, as cited in the manuscript
  Access      : https://www.genome.jp/kegg/
  Licence     : KEGG is provided under the KEGG access policy; academic use of
                the KEGG REST API is permitted, redistribution of the data is
                not.
  Used for    : pathway membership and pathway hierarchy.

STRING
  Version     : STRING v11, as cited in the manuscript
  Access      : https://string-db.org
  Licence     : Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International.
  Used for    : protein-protein interaction evidence and its confidence tier.

Hetionet
  Version     : Hetionet v1.0, from the systematic integration of biomedical
                knowledge cited as reference [15] of the manuscript
  Access      : https://github.com/hetio/hetionet
  Licence     : CC0 1.0 Universal.
  Used for    : cross-domain connections between node types.

SNOMED CT
  Version     : SNOMED CT international release, via a national Affiliate
                licence route
  Access      : https://www.snomed.org
  Licence     : SNOMED International Affiliate licence. Concept identifiers are
                used for type grounding only; no SNOMED CT content is
                redistributed with this release.
  Used for    : disease and morphology concept identity.

ICD-O-3 (International Classification of Diseases for Oncology, third edition)
  Version     : Third edition, second revision
  Access      : https://www.who.int/standards/classifications
  Licence     : World Health Organization terms of use.
  Used for    : morphology and topography coding of the disease nodes.

NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology — Melanoma: Cutaneous v2.2026
  Access      : https://www.nccn.org
  Licence     : Copyright National Comprehensive Cancer Network. The guideline
                text is not redistributed. The feasibility layer in
                src/pathanchor/guideline reads a caller-supplied statement
                table; no guideline text is shipped.
  Used for    : the feasibility set C(p) of Eq. (1).

GEO series GSE78220, GSE91061, GSE115821 / ENA study PRJEB23709
  Access      : see dataset_urls.txt
  Licence     : NCBI GEO and EBI ENA terms of use; each series additionally
                carries the terms of its originating publication.
  Used for    : the external validation profile table, which this release reads
                from a caller-supplied file and does not redistribute.

